<Base title="Photo & artwork credits — Kartik Tagore" description="Credits and licenses for photographs used in Kartik Tagore's personal website.">
  <article class="paper-document">
    <a class="breadcrumb" href="/">← Back to the workbench</a>
    <header class="article-head"><p class="eyebrow">Sources & thanks</p><h1>Photo & artwork credits</h1><p class="lede">Original sources behind the photographs and published illustrations.</p></header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>McQueen photography is from <a href="https://blog.sravjti.in/2026/10/20/mcqueen.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SRA VJTI's build article</a>, credited to the project team. The original SVGs are artwork created for this site.</p>
      <p>Curated public-domain and CC0 illustrations, when downloaded: <a href="https://freesvg.org/dumbbell-drawing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenClipart dumbbell drawing</a>; <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soccerball.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenClipart soccer ball</a>; <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Volleyball_(transparent).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Angelo Gelmi / Svgalbertian / Luan volleyball</a>; <a href="https://freesvg.org/shuttlecock" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">gnokii-based shuttlecock</a>; <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chess_white_knight.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CyrilKato / Sashité chess knight</a>; and <a href="https://freesvg.org/paddle" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenClipart table-tennis paddles</a>. The vector originals are publicly available artworks, not AI-rendered substitutes.</p>
      <p>Additional photographs, when enabled: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pair_of_8kg_dumbbells_(Unsplash).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cyril Saulnier / c_reel (dumbbells, CC0)</a>; <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soccer_ball.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Daniel Lobo (football, CC BY 2.0)</a>; <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Volleyball_Mikasa_2006.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tenisista97 (volleyball, CC BY-SA 3.0)</a>; <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shuttlecock.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BlackKnight (shuttlecock, public domain)</a>; <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chess_Piece,_Knight_MET_DP303335.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Metropolitan Museum of Art (knight, CC0)</a>; <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Table_tennis_racket_(51465161213).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jonas Perkuhn (table tennis, CC0)</a>; <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nvidia_Jetson_Nano_2_Development_Kit.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the Jetson Nano uploader (CC0)</a>.</p>
      <p>Photographs have been cropped, background-masked, and sometimes composited for the scrapbook layout. Licenses: <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY 2.0</a> · <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 3.0</a> · <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC0</a>.</p>
      <p>The separate manufacturer photographs supported by the optional preview script are <strong>not cleared for public use</strong> and should not be deployed without permission.</p>
      <p>The motorcycle helmet illustration was supplied as a downloaded PNG for this local preview. Its original creator and reuse license still need to be confirmed before publication.</p>
      <p>The Arduino UNO illustration was supplied as an SVG for this local preview. Its original creator and reuse license also need confirmation before publication; it replaces the earlier board artwork.</p>
      <p>The Jetson Nano render was supplied as a PNG. Its white backdrop has been removed and print grain and an irregular paper border added for this local preview. Original creator and reuse rights still need confirmation before publication.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
